  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-web-design",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What problem does it solve?",
      "text": "AI-generated prototype pages often include descriptions and sections you never asked for. Removing them can take repeated back-and-forth with the AI.\n\nThis DeepSeek Harness plugin lets you delete sections and edit text directly in the HTML preview, adjust styles and positions, and save the changes to the HTML file—without asking the AI to make each change."
    },
    {
      "section": "What problem does it solve?",
      "text": "In the plugin list, display names and descriptions follow the Harness language setting in English or Chinese (English is the default fallback); English names use the package name without its npm scope, Chinese names describe the purpose, and installation still uses the unchanged real package name."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile web add @guowenzhang/dsh-web-design\n```\n\nRestart DSH after installation. Open an `.html` or `.htm` file in the Sidebar, switch to **Edit**, click to select an element, and double-click to open its editor. After editing, click **Save to file**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- The HTML source changes only when you click **Save to file**. Preview edits are stored in `<filename>.design.json` beside the HTML file until then.\n- To change text, select the specific text element. Elements with multiple direct text runs cannot be replaced directly.\n- Elements generated by scripts or not uniquely locatable in the source are skipped when saving. Use unique, stable `id` values for editable elements and check the result after saving.\n- Relative CSS, JavaScript, image, and font references may not load in the preview. Single-file prototypes with inline styles and scripts are recommended."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[Apache-2.0](LICENSE); see also [NOTICE](NOTICE). The runtime dependencies `parse5` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-atomic-write` are both MIT-licensed."
    }
  ],
